            "review_title": "Review at Ca lang Toan Thang Restaurant",
            "review_text": "panasia\nMontreal, Canada134 contributions\n2\nBy the riverside\nMar 2016 • Friends\nHanoi is next to the Red river but you had never seen it except when travelling to the airport. This restaurant is not too far from Hoan Kiem lake were most of the restaurants catering to tourists are. Beautifully landscaping down the river bank with multilevel decks, the view is awesome! This restaurant is specialised in Lang fish preparation (fish native of the red river). There are 2 choices of live fishes: wild at 50$/kg or raised at 30$/kg. Most of them are from 2 to 5 kg range. They will prepare 3 or 4 dishes or soups to your liking. Our party choose a 2 kg fish and have it broiled over charcoal and the head made into soup, northern vietnamese style. They are well prepared and good. The bill came out to about 10$/person which is reasonable. This place is for food lovers who want something different than the westernized meals served in upscale restaurants around the old quarter. And you get the view and fresh air!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 11, 2016",
